    "body": "Correction to the earlier review: on this macOS host the `gpu_render` suite did **not** render. Every test requests `force_fallback_adapter: true`, macOS's Metal has no software fallback, and `device_and_queue()` returned `None`, so the 10 tests passed by skipping. The ortho fix stands on its math tests (`projection_tests`, including `the_ortho_depth_spans_zero_to_one_between_the_planes`, which checks near→0 and far→1). A real-render confirmation on macOS needs 615. The verdict is unchanged; only the evidence is corrected.",
